munication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew but he creates positive atmosphere? Actually A creates positive atmosphere with crew, but difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric may be contradictory. He also not willing to further education, which may affect adaptability.\n\nGiven the safety-critical nature, memory for numbers is a big issue. So B may be disqualified. C's attitude issues could be mitigated with training. A's communication difficulty and egocentric may also be problematic, but he is 100% reliable and creates positive atmosphere. However, lack of willingness to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nThus C seems strongest overall. Markus already argued for C. I can agree with C, but perhaps raise that C's unorganized and not good at taking criticism could affect safety. However, we can still recommend C, with a note that we need to address those issues.\n\nThus as Anna, I will align with Markus and vote for Candidate C. Provide reasoning: C's situational awareness and leadership outweigh attitude concerns, which can be mitigated. Also note that D's interpersonal issues are severe, B's memory issue is critical, A's communication issues also serious. So C is best.\n\nThus public message: I agree with Markus that C is best, explain why, mention concerns but manageable.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
